08,"disposition":"sustained","authority_weight":"high","url":"https://raymond-rishty.github.io/pca-ga/cases/ga36_2008__2007-08.html","raw_url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/raymond-rishty/pca-ga/main/cases/ga36_2008__2007-08.md","evidence_basis":"structured_case_metadata","relevance_status":"unreviewed","occurrences":[{"id":"bco:5-6--case:cases/ga36_2008__2007-08.md:occ-cc9d7fdf4566","url":"https://raymond-rishty.github.io/pca-ga/cases/ga36_2008__2007-08.html","repository_path":"cases/ga36_2008__2007-08.md","locator":{},"excerpt":"","sources":["judicial_cases.jsonl:bco_provisions"],"raw_url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/raymond-rishty/pca-ga/main/cases/ga36_2008__2007-08.md"}],"reference_presentation":{"group":"review","label":null},"metadata":{"topics":["constitutional_interpretation","differences_with_standards","westminster_standards","election","perseverance","apostasy","visible_invisible_church","baptism","presbytery_procedures","federal_vision","judicial_review","church_discipline"],"standard_of_review":"not_stated","case_numbers":["2007-8"],"body":"SJC","synopsis":"Louisiana Presbytery’s refusal to institute process after examining Steve Wilkins’s Federal Vision teachings was challenged for applying the wrong constitutional standard and overlooking a strong presumption that some views were out of conformity with the Westminster Standards. The SJC sustained the complaint and annulled Presbytery’s denial. A “difference” need not expressly contradict the Standards; Presbytery must independently investigate and classify it rather than accept the member’s assurance or shift the burden to objectors. The ruling did not adjudicate Wilkins’s guilt; the Central Carolina memorial remained before the SJC."}}],"history":[]}
